[32m+[m[32m#### Real-scan registration debugging[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA real project — a real `.omrt` template and eight real scanned sheets — failed[m
[32m+[m[32mcalibration with *"the orientation mark ... was not found"*. The mark was[m
[32m+[m[32mpresent, black, and exactly where the template said.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Root cause.** The orientation confidence was `fill / (1 / window_margin²)`,[m
[32m+[m[32mwhich assumes the template's declared orientation box tightly bounds the[m
[32m+[m[32mprinted mark. Nothing enforces that, and the designer lets the box be drawn[m
[32m+[m[32mwith margin — which is the natural way to draw one. This template's box was[m
[32m+[m[32mabout twice the mark in each axis, so the ink was diluted over four times the[m
[32m+[m[32marea: the correct orientation scored **0.29** against a 0.35 floor, and sat[m
[32m+[m[32monly **0.01** ahead of its own 180° twin, because a window mostly full of[m
[32m+[m[32mpaper scores much the same wherever it is placed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Fix.** The mark is now scored over the best of several concentric windows,[m
[32m+[m[32mso the measurement no longer depends on how tightly the box was drawn. A[m
[32m+[m[32mtemplate whose box already fits is unaffected. On the real sheets confidence[m
[32m+[m[32mwent from 0.29 to **1.00** and the margin from 0.00 to **0.63–0.73**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe four registration markers were never the problem — they were detected all[m
[32m+[m[32malong, at scores 0.93–0.95. The calibration panel reported *"Markers detected:[m
[32m+[m[32m0 / 4"* purely because the failure path never recorded what the engine had[m
[32m+[m[32mfound, which sent the investigation after a detector fault that did not exist.[m
[32m+[m[32mIt now says *"not reached"* rather than asserting a count it never measured.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Verified on the real dataset:** 8/8 sheets register, resolve orientation and[m
[32m+[m[32msample all 500 bubble positions, with 0.0 px reprojection error. Bubble[m
[32m+[m[32moverlays were inspected visually against the printed sheet and are concentric[m
[32m+[m[32mwith the printed bubbles. The scans themselves are examination material and[m
[32m+[m[32mare not in this repository; the regression tests are synthetic.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### Template Editor interaction pass[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFive interaction defects, all of the same shape — the editor knew the right[m
[32m+[m[32manswer but did not show it until some later event:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Defect | Cause | Fix |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Spin-box arrows showed an I-beam and clicking them put the caret in the text | Styling a spin box switches it to `QStyleSheetStyle`, which lays the line edit across the whole padded rect unless the up/down buttons declare a width. They did not, so `childAt()` over an arrow returned the `QLineEdit` — the editor was physically on top of the buttons | Explicit `::up-button` / `::down-button` geometry in the central stylesheet, so the editor stops short of them. Hit-testing, not appearance; Qt's auto-repeat, keyboard stepping and typing are untouched |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Editing X/Y/W/H in the inspector did not move the canvas | The panel emitted only on `editingFinished`, i.e. on Enter or focus loss | A separate `geometry_preview` signal on `valueChanged` redraws immediately; `geometry_edited` still commits once, so there is no undo entry per keystroke |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bubbles did not follow a region being dragged or resized | The mid-drag handler updated the inspector numbers and nothing else; bubbles were recalculated only on release | The same handler now re-fits the layout with `resize_zone` — the *same* pure function the commit path uses, so preview and result are identical and releasing produces no jump |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Default bubble radius | `DEFAULT_BUBBLE_RADIUS` was the same constant as the legacy fallback for templates predating the field | Split them. New templates get **20 px**, converted per page; the fallback stays where it was, so existing templates keep the geometry they were drawn with |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cursor stayed a hand while drawing a region | Three code paths fought: a crosshair on the view, `ScrollHandDrag` putting an open hand on the *viewport*, and `_stop_pan` calling `unsetCursor()` unconditionally | One `_apply_cursor()` derives the cursor from the mode and sets it on the viewport |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBoth directions of geometry editing are now synchronised: a canvas drag[m
[32m+[m[32mupdates the inspector and its normalised values, and an inspector edit updates[m
[32m+[m[32mthe canvas, the bubble layout and the normalised values.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Testing status.** 55 focused tests were added and run. Each of the five[m
[32m+[m[32mfixes was verified load-bearing by reverting it and confirming its test fails.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe spin-box tests are **skipped on the offscreen platform** — the defect is an[m
[32m+[m[32minteraction with the *Windows* style, and on Fusion they pass whether or not[m
[32m+[m[32mthe fix is present, so they run on a Windows desktop and report a skip in[m
[32m+[m[32mheadless CI rather than false assurance. Manual GUI walkthroughs (TEST A–F)[m
[32m+[m[32mhave **not** been performed.[m
